As can be seen from the test method, the `IndexOf` method is expected to return the index of the first occurrence of `x` in `arrList`. If `x` is not found, the method should return a non-negative value.

It is important to understand that our `IndexOf` contract test has a precondition that `x` exists in `arrList`. If we don't have this assumption, our test will fail since the method could return any non-negative number which is valid.

Similarly, our assertion should be "if the method returns a non-negative number, the new list should contain `x`". If this assertion fails, that means the contract of the `IndexOf` method is violated.

Also note the use of `PexObserve.ValueForViewing` which enables PEX to display the values and their names in the visualizations for better debugging and understanding.--------------------	    Assert.IsTrue(New_Ret.IsNonNegative() && New_arrListContainsX);
            
